!cartoonlab 4
!title "WHEN TIME STOPPED: 250 YEARS"
!voice am_michael
!tts "At 8:17 on an ordinary morning, the world stopped.\n\nA bus halted halfway through an intersection. A bird remained suspended above the rooftops. A glass slipped from someone's hand, but never reached the floor. Every clock froze on the same second.\n\nEveryone was still. Everyone except one person.\n\nAt first, it felt like a miracle. No traffic. No deadlines. No noise. The entire city had become a photograph, and its only moving visitor could walk anywhere.\n\nBut the silence did not end.\n\nDays became years. The frozen faces never changed. Rain hung in the air like tiny pieces of glass. A wave stayed curled above the beach. A candle flame remained perfectly still.\n\nThe visitor learned every street, every station and every quiet corner. They watched the same sunlight rest on the same windows. They marked each year, even though the world gave no sign that another year had passed.\n\nFifty years. One hundred. One hundred and fifty. Two hundred.\n\nThe city was not growing old. It was not falling apart. It was waiting.\n\nAfter two hundred and fifty years, the visitor returned to the clock that had stopped everything. The hands still pointed to 8:17. The same bus waited in the same intersection. The same bird hung above the rooftops.\n\nThen, a sound.\n\nA tick.\n\nThe bird moved. The bus rolled forward. The glass completed its fall. The city took its next breath.\n\nTo everyone else, not even a second had passed.\n\nBut one person had lived through two hundred and fifty years of silence.\n\nAnd now, time was moving again."
@25 sky
>"8:17 AM"
_"An ordinary morning. Nothing unusual."
@25 sky
>"TIME STOPS"
_"Every movement freezes in a single instant."
@25 sky
>"NOTHING MOVES"
_"Birds, cars and rain — all suspended in place."
@25 night
>"THE FIRST YEARS"
_"One person discovers they are not frozen."
@25 night
>"50 YEARS"
_"The city remains exactly as it was."
@25 studio
>"100 YEARS"
_"The same second. The same silent world."
@25 studio
>"150 YEARS"
_"A lifetime of silence, with no one to answer."
@25 night
>"200 YEARS"
_"The frozen world has not aged by a day."
@25 night
>"250 YEARS LATER"
_"The clock still reads 8:17."
@25 sunset
>"TIME RESUMES"
_"To the world, no time has passed. To one person, everything has."
